chapter.v:
of the 


sons of, 


Kohath, Uriel the chief, with 120 of his brothers;

of the 


sons of, 


Merari, Asaiah the chief, with 220 of his brothers;

of the 


sons of, 


Gershom, Joel the chief, with 130 of his brothers;

of the 


sons of, 


Elizaphan, Shemaiah the chief, with 200 of his brothers;

of the 


sons of, 


Hebron, Eliel the chief, with 80 of his brothers;

So the 


Levites appointed, 


Heman the son of Joel; and of his brothers Asaph the son of Berechiah; and of the sons of Merari, their brothers, Ethan the son of Kushaiah;

The singers, 


Heman, Asaph,, 


and Ethan, were to sound bronze cymbals;

Zechariah, Aziel, 


Shemiramoth, Jehiel,, 


Unni, Eliab, Maaseiah, and Benaiah were to play harps according to Alamoth;
